itle":"Orientation | Gustavus Adolphus College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3239,"longitude":-93.9705,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This stop applies during official New Student Orientation; the 2026 schedule is delivered through the Guidebook app.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-046","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Join an Orientation Group","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"Each new student is placed in a small Orientation Group led by a Gustie Greeter and faculty partner.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/admission-aid/new-students/orientation","source_title":"Orientation | Gustavus Adolphus College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3236,"longitude":-93.9722,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Participation details come from the current Orientation schedule; this is for incoming students.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-047","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Walk the official campus map route","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"The official campus map identifies the principal academic, student-life, arts, recreation, dining, library, and chapel buildings needed for a self-guided orientation walk.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/about/visitors/campus-map","source_title":"Campus Map | Gustavus Adolphus College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3236,"longitude":-93.9722,"maps_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=44.3236&mlon=-93.9722#map=16/44.3236/-93.9722","access_notes":"The map verifies locations, not that every building is open on weekends.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-048","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Explore the Arboretum trails","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"The campus Arboretum is free, open to all during daylight hours, and contains more than 2.5 miles of trails through three ecosystems.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/about/administrative-offices/arboretum","source_title":"Arboretum | Gustavus Adolphus College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3178,"longitude":-93.974,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Plan this stop before dusk and observe trail and weather conditions.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-049","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Locate the library and Student Union connection","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"The College locates Folke Bernadotte Memorial Library in the heart of campus connected to the Student Union.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/about/administrative-offices/library","source_title":"Library | Gustavus Adolphus College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3243,"longitude":-93.9717,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Weekend library access is limited: the published semester schedule lists Sunday noon–10 p.m. and no Saturday hours.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-050","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Visit Christ Chapel","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"Christ Chapel serves as a campus venue for worship, performances, community gatherings, and quiet reflection.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/about/facilities/christ-chapel","source_title":"Christ Chapel | Gustavus Adolphus College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3227,"longitude":-93.9717,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Be mindful of scheduled services, rehearsals, performances, and quiet use.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-051","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Check the Campus Activities Board program","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"The student-facing Campus Activities Board plans entertainment intended to serve the educational, cultural, social, and recreational needs of the Gustavus community.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/cao/programs.php/","source_title":"Program Overviews – Campus Activities","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.3239,"longitude":-93.9705,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This supports checking the current program, not assuming a free event occurs every weekend; event-specific access and cost vary.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"evidence_id":"gac-052","buckets":["college-first-weekend"],"subject_name":"Find first-year residence-hall common spaces","subject_type":"sequence_stop","supported_claim":"First-year students are assigned among designated options in Norelius or Pittman Hall, while Norelius is documented as having common lounges and study spaces.","source_url":"https://gustavus.edu/reslife/residences/index.php","source_title":"Residential Housing & Rates | Residences","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-12","latitude":44.326,"longitude":-93.974,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Residence halls are controlled-access living spaces; only residents and properly hosted guests should enter.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["The source footprint is too thin to mark the dossier complete: authoritative current sources support only a few genuinely late destinations in Saint Peter, and no additional restaurant was included without a direct current business source establishing under-21-safe late food service.","The off-campus street/district bucket is constrained by Saint Peter’s small scale and limited authoritative corridor-level documentation. Several records therefore use clearly bounded civic, park, or historic-district areas rather than inventing student districts or reducing the bucket to isolated businesses.","The input file states current_date 2026-08-13, while the execution environment date is 2026-08-12; source_fetched_at and researched_at use the execution environment’s date.","Many campus spaces do not publish room-level reservation or weekend-access rules. Their access_notes preserve those uncertainties rather than implying unrestricted availability.","The 2025–26 dining PDF is the strongest directly accessible source for Market Place evening service, but hours should be rechecked for later academic years and breaks."]}
